1
00:00:06,111 --> 00:00:07,738
[Jinman panting]

2
00:00:08,113 --> 00:00:11,241
[J] Long time no see, Jeong Jinman.

3
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:16,121
[Jinman grunting]

4
00:00:18,081 --> 00:00:20,459
[♪ tense music playing]

5
00:00:23,629 --> 00:00:26,673
[Jinman and J grunting]

6
00:00:28,842 --> 00:00:32,095
[J choking, gurgling]

7
00:00:39,269 --> 00:00:40,979
[knife slashing]

8
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:54,826
Q,

9
00:00:55,535 --> 00:00:59,081
unfortunately, the operation
that you've all been a part of

10
00:00:59,164 --> 00:01:00,957
will be temporarily suspended.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,293
[Marco] Suspended?

12
00:01:03,377 --> 00:01:04,586
What are you talking about?

13
00:01:04,669 --> 00:01:06,880
Even after losing J and X?

14
00:01:08,715 --> 00:01:09,716
Then…

15
00:01:12,177 --> 00:01:13,637
what about Jeong Jinman?

16
00:01:14,346 --> 00:01:16,014
[Jin] It's an order from the higher-ups.

17
00:01:16,098 --> 00:01:18,642
Securing the server is our priority.

18
00:01:19,476 --> 00:01:21,436
Babylon doesn't care if Jinman dies.

19
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,271
[scoffs]

20
00:01:25,315 --> 00:01:26,483
Priority?

21
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:30,946
It's best if you go back to Japan.

22
00:01:31,613 --> 00:01:33,699
[Jin] We need to send J back home as well.

23
00:01:35,158 --> 00:01:38,120
[♪ eerie tense music playing]

24
00:01:50,006 --> 00:01:57,013
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

25
00:02:01,017 --> 00:02:03,937
EPISODE 05
NEGOTIATION

26
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:05,772
[Jian] Woojin, hey!

27
00:02:05,856 --> 00:02:08,942
Don't close your eyes! No, you can't!

28
00:02:09,025 --> 00:02:10,819
-[muffled gunfire]
-[breathing heavily]

29
00:02:15,282 --> 00:02:18,577
[♪ gentle music playing]

30
00:02:30,088 --> 00:02:32,132
[birds chirping]

31
00:02:40,307 --> 00:02:41,808
[knocking on door]

32
00:02:43,643 --> 00:02:45,979
[nurse] Miss Arin? You're awake now.

33
00:02:48,231 --> 00:02:49,649
I'm not Miss Arin.

34
00:02:51,359 --> 00:02:52,360
What?

35
00:02:53,069 --> 00:02:54,362
It's Jian.

36
00:02:58,742 --> 00:02:59,785
Jeong Jian.

37
00:03:01,286 --> 00:03:02,454
[nurse] Uh…

38
00:03:04,998 --> 00:03:07,459
The doctor on duty will be here
in 30 minutes.

39
00:03:14,216 --> 00:03:16,510
Uh, please don't get up, Jian.
STYLE
::cue()

40
00:03:32,317 --> 00:03:33,902
[Jaewon] This is your new ID.

41
00:03:39,533 --> 00:03:42,827
-We've created a new identity for you.
-What about my uncle?

42
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:47,749
I'm pretty sure he was in my room earlier.

43
00:03:47,832 --> 00:03:50,877
You're right.
He was here a few minutes before you woke.

44
00:03:50,961 --> 00:03:52,879
But he had to take care of something,
so he left.

45
00:03:57,717 --> 00:03:59,636
SOCIAL SECURITY CARD
LEE YENA

46
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,807
I don't need the ID card.

47
00:04:04,474 --> 00:04:07,852
Changing identities is
kind of useless anyway.

48
00:04:09,229 --> 00:04:12,190
I'll just stay Jeong Jian.

49
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,819
[♪ gentle piano music playing]

50
00:04:18,071 --> 00:04:20,073
[Jaewon] I know you're still processing,

51
00:04:20,156 --> 00:04:22,117
but we've put together
a statement for you.

52
00:04:22,701 --> 00:04:24,953
The boat had been docked at the pier.

53
00:04:25,036 --> 00:04:28,582
Then Mr. Woojin brought you along
for the maintenance and inspection.

54
00:04:28,665 --> 00:04:31,042
We were out at sea
when the boat broke down.

55
00:04:33,044 --> 00:04:34,546
The reef punctured the boat.

56
00:04:35,463 --> 00:04:38,717
The ship started sinking
because water rushed in.

57
00:04:41,344 --> 00:04:43,722
I put on the life jacket
that was on board.

58
00:04:45,432 --> 00:04:46,433
But Woojin…

59
00:04:49,019 --> 00:04:51,521
thought he could save us
by fixing the engine.

60
00:04:53,523 --> 00:04:56,902
His leg got caught
in the damaged wheelhouse.

61
00:04:57,819 --> 00:04:59,863
He was dragged down with the boat.

62
00:05:03,867 --> 00:05:06,620
I lost… consciousness.

63
00:05:08,705 --> 00:05:10,206
I woke up in the hospital.

64
00:05:10,957 --> 00:05:13,043
All right, that's all for now.

65
00:05:14,044 --> 00:05:15,837
You can go, you must be exhausted.

66
00:05:17,839 --> 00:05:21,051
[sighs] Poor Woojin.
I can't believe this happened.

67
00:05:24,596 --> 00:05:26,932
[in Japanese] It's fortunate that it was
successful there in Thailand at least.

68
00:05:28,433 --> 00:05:29,643
For now, take the recovered items and…

69
00:05:29,726 --> 00:05:30,769
[door opening]

70
00:05:32,812 --> 00:05:33,855
[door closes]

71
00:05:37,275 --> 00:05:39,444
Take the recovered item
and return to Korea.

72
00:05:39,527 --> 00:05:40,737
[call-ending beep]

73
00:05:42,822 --> 00:05:48,036
Honestly, people in this country
have no basic manners.

74
00:05:51,748 --> 00:05:52,832
[in English] What's going on?

75
00:05:52,916 --> 00:05:54,125
Uh…

76
00:05:57,545 --> 00:05:58,546
It's, uh…

77
00:05:58,630 --> 00:06:02,676
Black Mountain Alliance has received
organized support for years

78
00:06:02,759 --> 00:06:05,637
from a private military company
named Babylon.

79
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:08,431
Clashes between militant
factions are now spreading

80
00:06:08,515 --> 00:06:10,225
into neighboring regions.

81
00:06:10,308 --> 00:06:12,143
-Authorities are treating…
-That's not, uh…

82
00:06:12,811 --> 00:06:13,937
That's not all.

83
00:06:14,771 --> 00:06:18,108
The assassinations of the high-ranking
government officials have escalated.

84
00:06:19,567 --> 00:06:21,528
According to sources,
there is a possibility

85
00:06:21,611 --> 00:06:23,780
that this was a strategic operation.

86
00:06:23,863 --> 00:06:26,032
The evidence is leading
to a private organization--

87
00:06:26,116 --> 00:06:28,076
[reporter] We are joined today
by an expert in the field.

88
00:06:28,159 --> 00:06:30,954
The weapons North Korea unveiled
at the Victory Day parade

89
00:06:31,037 --> 00:06:32,664
have been significantly upgraded.

90
00:06:33,456 --> 00:06:34,708
Jeong Jinman.

91
00:06:37,502 --> 00:06:40,797
That disgusting parasite.
STYLE
::cue()

92
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:08,491
[indistinct chatter]

93
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,257
[♪ somber music playing]

94
00:07:33,683 --> 00:07:34,684
[Jeomrye] Arin.

95
00:07:59,959 --> 00:08:00,960
Arin…

96
00:08:02,879 --> 00:08:04,756
are you blaming yourself?

97
00:08:08,551 --> 00:08:10,094
[sobs softly]

98
00:08:11,304 --> 00:08:14,933
Most of the aunties here
have lost their husbands

99
00:08:15,016 --> 00:08:17,477
because something
happened to them out at sea.

100
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:21,189
They see it as their fate.

101
00:08:23,066 --> 00:08:24,108
It's life.

102
00:08:24,192 --> 00:08:25,318
I'm sorry.

103
00:08:25,568 --> 00:08:27,070
[sobbing]

104
00:08:27,195 --> 00:08:29,447
Auntie, really, I'm sorry.

105
00:08:31,282 --> 00:08:32,784
I'm sorry.

106
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:34,661
I'm sorry.

107
00:08:34,744 --> 00:08:36,871
I'm sorry, Auntie.

108
00:08:37,664 --> 00:08:39,165
So sorry.

109
00:08:41,042 --> 00:08:43,753
[♪ somber music continues]

110
00:08:48,967 --> 00:08:50,260
Listen well.

111
00:08:50,343 --> 00:08:54,514
You're blaming yourself,
but it won't bring Woojin back.

112
00:08:55,431 --> 00:08:58,518
You need to keep living your own life.
Understand?

113
00:09:00,478 --> 00:09:03,523
I know it's hard right now,
but when you look back,

114
00:09:03,606 --> 00:09:07,026
you'll see that
this is just a moment in your life.

115
00:09:08,153 --> 00:09:09,279
You must be brave.

116
00:09:09,821 --> 00:09:12,323
Make sure to live tenaciously and be bold.

117
00:09:13,032 --> 00:09:15,577
You'll heal Arin by living a good life.

118
00:09:16,578 --> 00:09:19,706
[continues sobbing]

119
00:09:28,423 --> 00:09:29,465
We're all right.

120
00:09:31,384 --> 00:09:32,510
Don't worry about us here.

121
00:09:34,095 --> 00:09:35,096
Just live.

122
00:09:36,764 --> 00:09:37,807
Arin, go.

123
00:09:39,684 --> 00:09:40,977
Forget about us.

124
00:09:42,979 --> 00:09:44,355
Live your life.

125
00:10:02,290 --> 00:10:03,583
[L] You'll be all right alone?

126
00:10:09,214 --> 00:10:10,423
We'll come back tomorrow.
STYLE
::cue()

127
00:10:12,634 --> 00:10:15,553
[♪ tense somber music playing]

128
00:10:57,387 --> 00:10:58,429
Now…

129
00:11:01,474 --> 00:11:03,226
I'm all alone.

130
00:11:15,613 --> 00:11:18,199
[Q crying]

131
00:11:18,825 --> 00:11:21,536
[♪ music slowly turns foreboding]

132
00:11:25,456 --> 00:11:28,042
[breathing heavily]

133
00:11:34,590 --> 00:11:37,677
[sighs, sniffles]

134
00:11:51,149 --> 00:11:52,317
[Q] Jeong Jinman…

135
00:11:54,736 --> 00:11:56,738
this is the darkness you created.

136
00:11:59,532 --> 00:12:01,200
I will make you pay for it.

137
00:12:02,493 --> 00:12:04,370
[♪ music crescendos]

138
00:12:04,871 --> 00:12:05,872
[♪ music ends]

139
00:12:14,047 --> 00:12:16,924
You and your brother,
you've always been good kids.

140
00:12:18,092 --> 00:12:21,387
From when he was this tall
and you were this tall.

141
00:12:22,930 --> 00:12:23,973
I'm in your debt.

142
00:12:24,807 --> 00:12:26,934
Sir, thank you for the past few days.

143
00:12:30,605 --> 00:12:31,689
Ichika…

144
00:12:33,566 --> 00:12:36,694
reach out to me anytime you need.

145
00:12:41,074 --> 00:12:42,283
I appreciate it.

146
00:12:48,164 --> 00:12:49,374
Thank you so much.

147
00:12:51,042 --> 00:12:52,043
Be strong.

148
00:12:53,336 --> 00:12:56,130
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

149
00:13:14,649 --> 00:13:16,234
Is M still in Thailand?

150
00:13:16,984 --> 00:13:18,945
He's back in Korea with the asset.

151
00:13:20,696 --> 00:13:23,157
-He apologized for not being here.
-Yeah.

152
00:13:26,452 --> 00:13:28,162
Thank you for being here.

153
00:13:28,246 --> 00:13:29,414
So what now?

154
00:13:33,209 --> 00:13:34,961
Let's go back to Korea.

155
00:13:38,089 --> 00:13:41,134
I'm going to murder Jeong Jinman
with my own hands.
STYLE
::cue()

156
00:13:42,385 --> 00:13:45,805
[♪ tense music playing]

157
00:14:16,627 --> 00:14:18,754
[worker] Hey, you're gonna
have to wait, okay?

158
00:14:20,339 --> 00:14:22,175
[indistinct chatter]

159
00:14:31,809 --> 00:14:33,269
[worker] Thank you. Thank you so much.

160
00:14:51,704 --> 00:14:52,747
[mouse clicks]

161
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:54,123
[door opening]

162
00:14:54,248 --> 00:14:55,499
[security camera whirs]

163
00:14:55,583 --> 00:14:56,751
[door closes]

164
00:14:56,834 --> 00:15:00,463
Boss, a lot of orders
from the Philippines are coming in.

165
00:15:00,796 --> 00:15:01,797
Hm?

166
00:15:03,549 --> 00:15:04,550
Oh!

167
00:15:11,307 --> 00:15:12,433
Jeong Jian!

168
00:15:14,018 --> 00:15:16,020
[♪ soft music playing]

169
00:15:25,029 --> 00:15:26,197
[Jian] When did you move in?

170
00:15:26,364 --> 00:15:29,450
Uh… We've been preparing this whole time,

171
00:15:29,533 --> 00:15:32,787
but it's only been about ten days
since we settled in.

172
00:15:32,870 --> 00:15:33,871
[lock clicks]

173
00:15:35,498 --> 00:15:38,793
[digital trills]

174
00:15:38,876 --> 00:15:40,002
[lock beeping, clicking]

175
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,051
[thuds]

176
00:15:49,887 --> 00:15:50,888
I'll carry it.

177
00:15:50,972 --> 00:15:53,224
-I've got it.
-Okay.

178
00:15:55,059 --> 00:15:58,062
[mechanical whirring]

179
00:16:00,773 --> 00:16:01,774
[thuds]

180
00:16:07,238 --> 00:16:10,449
I'm really glad that
you didn't get hurt, Jeong Jian.

181
00:16:11,617 --> 00:16:14,745
Jeong Jinman is… here, right?

182
00:16:15,997 --> 00:16:20,960
Mm-hmm. The boss was really
worried about you.

183
00:16:26,424 --> 00:16:29,343
[♪ pensive music playing]

184
00:16:44,525 --> 00:16:45,526
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

185
00:17:01,876 --> 00:17:02,960
[bag thuds]

186
00:17:05,338 --> 00:17:06,672
[Jian] You're okay, right?

187
00:17:06,756 --> 00:17:08,716
[sighs in relief]

188
00:17:08,799 --> 00:17:10,051
So glad you're here.

189
00:17:10,885 --> 00:17:13,262
[♪ soft tense music playing]

190
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:26,484
[mechanical whirring]

191
00:17:28,486 --> 00:17:29,487
[thuds]

192
00:17:51,425 --> 00:17:53,344
This will be your room for the time being.

193
00:17:54,845 --> 00:17:57,848
Oh, great. No windows for me.

194
00:17:58,766 --> 00:18:01,519
Yeah. Obviously. It's a basement.

195
00:18:07,983 --> 00:18:11,612
Take some time to rest.
You're probably exhausted.

196
00:18:17,410 --> 00:18:19,078
I tried to decorate it like our old place.

197
00:18:19,161 --> 00:18:20,663
It reminds me of that day.

198
00:18:23,416 --> 00:18:25,084
It's not exactly the same, right?

199
00:18:25,751 --> 00:18:27,336
No cameras in my room this time?

200
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:35,803
You made the right choice.

201
00:18:37,638 --> 00:18:39,932
Thanks for coming back, Jeong Jian.

202
00:18:42,017 --> 00:18:43,894
I didn't come back to make you happy.

203
00:19:08,544 --> 00:19:09,545
[sighs]

204
00:19:09,628 --> 00:19:11,172
You scared me.

205
00:19:13,674 --> 00:19:14,884
You should stop.

206
00:19:16,051 --> 00:19:18,345
Boss, I said, we shouldn't put
a camera in there.

207
00:19:18,429 --> 00:19:19,472
Wait a sec.

208
00:19:20,473 --> 00:19:24,935
That camera was already installed there.
You decided to make that Jian's room.

209
00:19:25,019 --> 00:19:26,771
That's not important.

210
00:19:26,854 --> 00:19:29,523
Don't think about continuing
to spy on her.

211
00:19:29,607 --> 00:19:33,027
-Hey. Look. Do me a favor.
-Huh?

212
00:19:33,986 --> 00:19:36,363
Get rid of it before she notices.

213
00:19:37,448 --> 00:19:39,617
-This guy…
-[sighs] Thanks.

214
00:19:43,913 --> 00:19:45,456
[inhales deeply]

215
00:19:50,836 --> 00:19:52,588
[cries softly]

216
00:20:01,889 --> 00:20:04,225
[♪ soft somber music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

217
00:20:17,530 --> 00:20:19,532
[phone buzzing]

218
00:20:41,554 --> 00:20:46,058
[Babylon executive 1] This information
leak cost about 20 billion dollars.

219
00:20:46,141 --> 00:20:48,853
What will happen if they find out

220
00:20:48,936 --> 00:20:52,523
we supplied the weapons
to both the government and the rebels?

221
00:20:52,606 --> 00:20:54,358
[sighs irritably]

222
00:20:54,650 --> 00:20:58,487
The rebels aren't the problem right now.
What do you think North Korea would do?

223
00:20:58,571 --> 00:21:01,031
The US government won't just sit back
and do nothing.

224
00:21:01,824 --> 00:21:05,953
The Korean branch dropped the ball.
I'm here to recover it.

225
00:21:06,036 --> 00:21:07,121
[Babylon executive 2] Nonsense!

226
00:21:07,204 --> 00:21:08,789
Take some responsibility!

227
00:21:09,498 --> 00:21:11,000
[Chen] However…

228
00:21:11,083 --> 00:21:14,128
didn't this highly confidential
information become public

229
00:21:14,211 --> 00:21:16,130
because your operation failed?

230
00:21:16,213 --> 00:21:20,009
The operation failure
was entirely my responsibility.

231
00:21:21,176 --> 00:21:23,846
Good job, everyone.
I'll take it from here.

232
00:21:27,349 --> 00:21:29,518
[Chen] You were careless
and moved impulsively.

233
00:21:29,602 --> 00:21:31,770
Did you stop to think about
what will happen

234
00:21:31,854 --> 00:21:35,357
if Jeong Jinman decides to leak
other confidential information?

235
00:21:37,651 --> 00:21:39,236
I apologize for my actions.

236
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,697
Do you think that I can't see through you?

237
00:21:42,489 --> 00:21:44,074
Your self-interest is clear.

238
00:21:44,742 --> 00:21:49,997
You're planning to use the murthehelp app
to conduct your own business, are you not?

239
00:21:50,539 --> 00:21:54,460
I'm not, sir. I only have
Babylon's best interests in mind.

240
00:21:54,543 --> 00:21:58,255
I understand. I've read the report too.

241
00:21:58,339 --> 00:22:01,508
I get that it's
a very attractive business model.

242
00:22:02,509 --> 00:22:04,970
But that should not be our first priority.

243
00:22:05,429 --> 00:22:06,430
Correct?

244
00:22:07,973 --> 00:22:11,143
We have no interest
in that cockroach Jeong Jinman.

245
00:22:11,226 --> 00:22:14,438
Whether you decide to kill him
or buy him, do what you please.

246
00:22:14,521 --> 00:22:16,523
We need you to prioritize.

247
00:22:16,607 --> 00:22:18,609
You are to retrieve the server first.

248
00:22:18,692 --> 00:22:20,486
Your message is received.

249
00:22:20,569 --> 00:22:24,406
[Chen] Regarding the murthehelp system,
I will leave it to your discretion

250
00:22:24,490 --> 00:22:27,242
on how to take over and move forward
with the business.

251
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:32,998
If you are successful, I will entrust
the entirety of Babylon Korea to you.

252
00:22:33,999 --> 00:22:36,418
[♪ tense music playing]

253
00:22:41,256 --> 00:22:44,134
[Minhye] She's staying in a hotel
that's not very far from Babylon.

254
00:22:45,678 --> 00:22:49,390
[Jinwoo] Since it's just a regular hotel,
it should be fairly easy to gain access.

255
00:22:52,768 --> 00:22:55,187
[Minhye] I guarantee
it won't be as easy as you think.

256
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,606
[guide, in Chinese]
We will have breakfast together.

257
00:22:57,690 --> 00:23:01,944
And depart at eight o'clock sharp tomorrow
to begin our sightseeing schedule.

258
00:23:02,027 --> 00:23:05,364
Depart at eight o'clock. Understood!

259
00:23:05,447 --> 00:23:11,203
That's all for today's schedule
and you can rest in your rooms.

260
00:23:11,912 --> 00:23:13,163
[camera shutters click rapidly]

261
00:23:13,372 --> 00:23:17,501
[guide] The convenience store is
on the first floor

262
00:23:17,584 --> 00:23:19,795
and you can use it freely, anytime.

263
00:23:27,594 --> 00:23:28,595
[elevator chimes]

264
00:23:38,689 --> 00:23:39,732
[in English] Why are you up here?

265
00:23:39,815 --> 00:23:42,985
[in Chinese] Huh? Where's everybody?

266
00:23:43,068 --> 00:23:45,279
Strange. Did I get off on the wrong floor?

267
00:23:45,362 --> 00:23:48,157
[in English] This floor is fully booked
for conference participants only.

268
00:23:49,908 --> 00:23:50,909
[Minhye, in Chinese] Really?

269
00:23:50,993 --> 00:23:51,994
[bodyguard, in English] I'm sorry?

270
00:23:52,578 --> 00:23:54,580
[in Chinese] It's nothing. Nothing.
I didn't understand.

271
00:23:54,663 --> 00:23:58,208
Oh, it's okay.
Wow, but you're really tall, aren't you?

272
00:23:59,209 --> 00:24:00,377
[in English] What's going on?

273
00:24:00,461 --> 00:24:02,504
A Chinese tourist came up here by mistake.

274
00:24:09,762 --> 00:24:11,346
[Minhye] It looks like that woman
and her little sidekick

275
00:24:11,430 --> 00:24:13,015
are staying on the same floor.

276
00:24:14,099 --> 00:24:15,768
Should I eliminate them when I can?

277
00:24:17,102 --> 00:24:18,771
I can probably do it pretty easily.

278
00:24:20,814 --> 00:24:21,857
No, thanks.

279
00:24:23,067 --> 00:24:27,029
Even if you eliminate them, Babylon will
just keep sending their replacements.

280
00:24:27,112 --> 00:24:28,906
Do you know her?

281
00:24:29,948 --> 00:24:32,201
When I was in the special forces,

282
00:24:32,284 --> 00:24:35,037
we had an operation to rescue hostages
in Southeast Asia.

283
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,955
That's the only time we've met.

284
00:24:37,706 --> 00:24:40,667
There were Koreans
amongst the Japanese hostages.
STYLE
::cue()

285
00:24:40,751 --> 00:24:43,712
Since Japan couldn't deploy troops,
Babylon was called in.

286
00:24:44,755 --> 00:24:47,007
You said, in Hanam-do,
the Babylon team leader was

287
00:24:47,091 --> 00:24:48,175
a Japanese woman, right?

288
00:24:52,221 --> 00:24:55,516
If memory serves correct,
her code name is Q.

289
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:58,102
[♪ soft pensive music playing]

290
00:24:58,185 --> 00:24:59,520
[sighs]

291
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:03,148
Cheolseung,
look into the team leader and Q,

292
00:25:03,232 --> 00:25:05,943
and include all of their team members
that entered Korea.

293
00:25:06,026 --> 00:25:07,945
Get all the detailed information you can.

294
00:25:08,779 --> 00:25:09,988
[Q] I'm Q.

295
00:25:10,072 --> 00:25:12,616
The next time we meet,
we'll go have a drink together.

296
00:25:12,699 --> 00:25:14,118
[in Japanese] Thank you.

297
00:25:14,201 --> 00:25:16,537
[in English]
Long time no see, Jeong Jinman.

298
00:25:17,121 --> 00:25:18,497
[phone buzzing]

299
00:25:28,715 --> 00:25:29,758
ATTORNEY JANG INSEOP

300
00:25:29,842 --> 00:25:32,261
[Cheolseung]
"Negotiation requested." [scoffs]

301
00:25:32,386 --> 00:25:35,722
Those dumb assholes always have
to fuck around and find out the hard way.

302
00:25:35,806 --> 00:25:37,307
[Jinwoo] We can't do this now.

303
00:25:37,391 --> 00:25:39,143
We don't have enough manpower.

304
00:25:39,226 --> 00:25:41,270
Code Yellow took heavy losses
on Hanam-do Island.

305
00:25:41,353 --> 00:25:43,063
Our Code Reds are scattered.

306
00:25:43,147 --> 00:25:45,274
They're waiting to see what happens.

307
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:50,154
Right, it could be dangerous.
It's not time to negotiate.

308
00:25:50,237 --> 00:25:53,157
Let's secure a safe house first.
And then we can move Jian.

309
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:54,867
[Jian] Am I some kind of object?

310
00:25:55,742 --> 00:25:57,536
Move me wherever you want?

311
00:25:59,288 --> 00:26:00,956
Over and over.

312
00:26:01,039 --> 00:26:02,583
Without ever negotiating.

313
00:26:05,127 --> 00:26:07,087
You hide, then fight and move.

314
00:26:07,171 --> 00:26:10,007
You repeat the cycle again and again.
And then what?

315
00:26:10,591 --> 00:26:12,843
How many people are gonna die
to protect me?

316
00:26:14,219 --> 00:26:18,307
Do you even know
how many people on Hanam-do Island died?

317
00:26:19,975 --> 00:26:21,018
[scoffs]

318
00:26:22,394 --> 00:26:26,023
When Uncle Jinwoo dies
and Minhye Eonni dies, does this end?

319
00:26:27,357 --> 00:26:28,817
I won't accept that.

320
00:26:28,901 --> 00:26:31,528
I'm not allowing any of you
to sacrifice yourselves.

321
00:26:33,238 --> 00:26:34,323
Do you understand?

322
00:26:38,202 --> 00:26:39,620
That's why I came back.

323
00:26:50,464 --> 00:26:54,009
All right. What's your plan, then?

324
00:26:54,760 --> 00:26:57,304
What are you going to do
to prevent all of us…

325
00:26:58,096 --> 00:26:59,348
from being sacrificed?

326
00:27:00,849 --> 00:27:02,100
Whatever I can.

327
00:27:02,184 --> 00:27:03,518
[scoffs]

328
00:27:07,397 --> 00:27:08,649
Listen up, Jeong Jian.

329
00:27:10,359 --> 00:27:12,861
It's not possible to negotiate
without strength.

330
00:27:13,737 --> 00:27:15,530
You can't just talk a big game.

331
00:27:15,614 --> 00:27:18,450
You better put your money
where your mouth is first.

332
00:27:18,533 --> 00:27:19,743
You need to prove it.

333
00:27:21,245 --> 00:27:22,329
Hm.

334
00:27:22,788 --> 00:27:23,830
I get it.

335
00:27:25,582 --> 00:27:26,708
I'll prove it to you.

336
00:27:28,543 --> 00:27:30,045
Tell me what to do, I'll do it.

337
00:27:30,837 --> 00:27:33,840
[rain pouring]

338
00:27:35,509 --> 00:27:37,761
[♪ tense music playing]

339
00:27:45,978 --> 00:27:48,772
[voicemail] The customer you have dialed
cannot answer your call.

340
00:27:48,855 --> 00:27:50,816
Please hang up and try the call again.

341
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:56,196
[Jian] No umbrella?

342
00:27:58,115 --> 00:28:00,701
I forgot my umbrella all the time
when I was little.

343
00:28:05,497 --> 00:28:06,873
[chuckles softly]

344
00:28:08,083 --> 00:28:10,419
See this? Do you want one?

345
00:28:14,006 --> 00:28:15,048
Try them on.

346
00:28:20,303 --> 00:28:23,473
It's all right. You can trust me.

347
00:28:24,641 --> 00:28:26,101
I'm friends with your father.

348
00:28:28,603 --> 00:28:29,688
[chuckles softly]

349
00:28:30,147 --> 00:28:31,314
[Jian] What?

350
00:28:31,398 --> 00:28:33,400
-[Jian] Oh, no.
-[child] Why are you so bad at this?

351
00:28:34,192 --> 00:28:36,361
[Jian] Why are you so good at this?

352
00:28:36,445 --> 00:28:37,571
-You--
-[child] Shoot!

353
00:28:37,779 --> 00:28:38,989
[car horn honking]

354
00:28:39,656 --> 00:28:41,575
Oh, hey. It's my dad.

355
00:28:56,131 --> 00:28:58,633
-General Suho!
-Hi, Dad!

356
00:29:00,719 --> 00:29:02,262
Where did you get this raincoat?

357
00:29:03,764 --> 00:29:06,725
Your friend. She gave me an extra one.
STYLE
::cue()

358
00:29:07,184 --> 00:29:09,061
Hm? My friend?

359
00:29:14,524 --> 00:29:17,194
Mr. Lee Jaeyoon. It's good to see you.

360
00:29:19,154 --> 00:29:20,655
Oh, it's been a while.

361
00:29:20,739 --> 00:29:22,532
Good to see you too. Hey.

362
00:29:23,533 --> 00:29:25,368
Suho, jump in the car, wait for Dad.

363
00:29:26,369 --> 00:29:28,830
[Suho] Thank you for the raincoat.
See you later.

364
00:29:28,914 --> 00:29:29,915
[Jian] Bye.

365
00:29:32,084 --> 00:29:35,003
[thunder rumbling]

366
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:45,514
[Jian groans]

367
00:29:45,597 --> 00:29:47,849
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

368
00:29:49,101 --> 00:29:51,520
What do you want? Why are you here?

369
00:29:51,603 --> 00:29:54,481
-[strained] Jeong Jian.
-Speak louder.

370
00:29:55,482 --> 00:29:58,735
[strained]
I'm Jeong Jian, Jeong Jinman's niece.

371
00:29:58,819 --> 00:30:01,613
Jeong Jian? Code Green?

372
00:30:03,990 --> 00:30:06,118
[Jian grunts, coughs]

373
00:30:06,868 --> 00:30:08,411
Did Jinman send you?

374
00:30:08,495 --> 00:30:12,457
That guy's a total scumbag.
He sent you after my son?

375
00:30:13,250 --> 00:30:15,794
It's pretty funny hearing
the word scumbag…

376
00:30:17,170 --> 00:30:19,172
-come out of your mouth.
-What?

377
00:30:19,923 --> 00:30:20,924
[sighs]

378
00:30:23,718 --> 00:30:26,930
The day Mr. Kim betrayed us
and brought all the Code Reds to attack.

379
00:30:27,889 --> 00:30:29,266
Why weren't you there?

380
00:30:29,349 --> 00:30:30,600
[scoffs]

381
00:30:31,434 --> 00:30:33,228
Did Jinman send you
to confront me about this?

382
00:30:34,312 --> 00:30:35,313
No.

383
00:30:36,273 --> 00:30:39,192
I didn't come here
to argue with you, all right?

384
00:30:40,026 --> 00:30:41,444
I'm here for a reason.

385
00:30:41,528 --> 00:30:45,365
Only two people on this Earth can persuade
the Code Reds to move.

386
00:30:45,448 --> 00:30:48,201
My uncle said one of them was Mr. Kim,
but he's dead.

387
00:30:49,619 --> 00:30:50,829
That's why I'm here.

388
00:30:51,621 --> 00:30:54,082
The only other person is you,
Mr. Ahn Seongbeom.

389
00:30:55,375 --> 00:30:58,879
-Will you please persuade the Code Reds?
-Maybe you haven't heard.

390
00:31:00,422 --> 00:31:01,590
[Seongbeom] I'm retired.

391
00:31:03,008 --> 00:31:04,050
[Jian] Wait.

392
00:31:05,677 --> 00:31:07,179
Aren't you even curious?

393
00:31:09,848 --> 00:31:11,308
I found your son.

394
00:31:12,184 --> 00:31:13,852
I knew who you were…

395
00:31:14,769 --> 00:31:16,479
and what your alias was.

396
00:31:19,149 --> 00:31:20,483
You know what's cool?

397
00:31:21,318 --> 00:31:25,447
I offered the Code Purples extra money
to give me info on you, but they declined.

398
00:31:25,530 --> 00:31:29,034
They said it's an unwritten rule.
Never touch family.

399
00:31:30,327 --> 00:31:33,079
Every one of them refused to say anything.

400
00:31:33,830 --> 00:31:37,292
So how do you think it is
that I found out who you were…

401
00:31:38,084 --> 00:31:40,295
and exactly where your son was?

402
00:31:48,511 --> 00:31:52,098
Babylon's been collecting
personal information on every Code Red.

403
00:31:52,182 --> 00:31:55,227
Those assholes put every single one
of you under surveillance.

404
00:31:56,186 --> 00:31:57,229
[angrily] Why?

405
00:32:03,652 --> 00:32:04,819
Tell me why!

406
00:32:05,278 --> 00:32:07,906
I'm retired!
Why is Babylon digging up my information?

407
00:32:07,989 --> 00:32:09,574
Why do you think, huh?

408
00:32:10,450 --> 00:32:11,743
It's always about money.

409
00:32:11,826 --> 00:32:13,870
Babylon is a big corporation

410
00:32:13,954 --> 00:32:16,081
and they're trying to swallow murthehelp,
to take over.

411
00:32:16,957 --> 00:32:18,416
I'll be blunt with you.

412
00:32:19,209 --> 00:32:22,754
The Babylon division from Japan
came to take murthehelp from us.

413
00:32:23,672 --> 00:32:25,799
They've been trying to mobilize Code Reds.

414
00:32:26,424 --> 00:32:29,970
They've even created a fake app
and are recruiting people without codes.

415
00:32:32,264 --> 00:32:34,099
They'll probably start a war with us.

416
00:32:35,058 --> 00:32:36,726
We don't have enough manpower.

417
00:32:37,852 --> 00:32:38,895
We need your help.

418
00:32:44,734 --> 00:32:46,528
Jeong Jinman, you listening?

419
00:32:46,611 --> 00:32:47,946
Your niece has guts.

420
00:32:48,613 --> 00:32:51,574
But if you ever try to send anyone
to my son again,

421
00:32:51,658 --> 00:32:52,909
I promise you,

422
00:32:52,993 --> 00:32:56,871
I'll have no problems tearing apart
and killing both you and your niece.

423
00:32:56,955 --> 00:33:00,458
The only reason I'm holding back now
is as a final courtesy to you

424
00:33:00,542 --> 00:33:02,294
as an old colleague of mine.

425
00:33:04,087 --> 00:33:07,424
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

426
00:33:15,390 --> 00:33:16,516
[Jian sighs]

427
00:33:16,891 --> 00:33:18,560
[Jian] I think I messed it up.

428
00:33:19,978 --> 00:33:21,354
Please come and get me.
STYLE
::cue()

429
00:33:37,454 --> 00:33:40,790
You won't be able to change
Ahn Seongbeom's mind that easily.

430
00:33:40,874 --> 00:33:41,875
Don't give up yet.

431
00:33:43,418 --> 00:33:45,920
I didn't go to see his son
to threaten his family.

432
00:33:47,339 --> 00:33:48,798
[sighs]

433
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:51,885
It just backfired.

434
00:33:52,886 --> 00:33:54,054
Jian…

435
00:33:55,597 --> 00:33:57,474
you probably feel that

436
00:33:57,557 --> 00:34:01,061
your uncle really messed up your life
by involving you in all of this.

437
00:34:01,144 --> 00:34:02,812
But he really does care.

438
00:34:02,896 --> 00:34:05,940
And trust me, he understands
the pain of losing someone you love.

439
00:34:07,525 --> 00:34:10,737
Jinman's lost a lot of people
in every stage of his life.

440
00:34:10,820 --> 00:34:14,866
As a soldier, a mercenary,
and long after leaving Babylon.

441
00:34:16,701 --> 00:34:17,827
It's been hard.

442
00:34:19,329 --> 00:34:21,790
Jinman's experienced so much loss that…

443
00:34:22,499 --> 00:34:25,960
at some point he just accepted
this endless cycle of pain.

444
00:34:26,044 --> 00:34:28,713
That's why he's so guarded with everyone.

445
00:34:31,341 --> 00:34:34,094
Your uncle wanted you
to be strong and resilient.

446
00:34:34,844 --> 00:34:37,597
He just doesn't want you
to end up like he did.

447
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:40,850
I don't want to end up like him either.

448
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,607
I'm not going to do things like he did.

449
00:34:49,234 --> 00:34:50,235
Ever.

450
00:35:11,798 --> 00:35:13,591
I heard that you want to spar with me.

451
00:35:13,675 --> 00:35:15,343
Since Master Pasin's not here--

452
00:35:16,052 --> 00:35:17,429
[groans]

453
00:35:22,308 --> 00:35:24,686
[♪ upbeat music playing]

454
00:35:30,442 --> 00:35:33,945
Inventory check is the basics
of running the shopping mall.

455
00:35:35,029 --> 00:35:38,158
Finish all of this today
and make sure you get it inspected.

456
00:35:40,744 --> 00:35:42,287
[Minhye grunts]

457
00:35:42,370 --> 00:35:43,955
[Jian grunts]

458
00:35:44,038 --> 00:35:45,457
[Jinwoo] This is 9 mm.

459
00:35:45,540 --> 00:35:47,417
This is 5.56,

460
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:49,586
and this is 7.62.

461
00:35:49,669 --> 00:35:53,882
Simply put, the larger the caliber,
the more damage it does.

462
00:35:54,007 --> 00:35:56,593
[gunshots]

463
00:35:57,886 --> 00:35:59,929
[Minhye] A longer barrel
increases the range.

464
00:36:00,638 --> 00:36:03,600
When the sun's in front of you,
close the scope cover

465
00:36:04,476 --> 00:36:05,560
and look in the middle.

466
00:36:06,519 --> 00:36:09,063
Or you'll give yourself away
because of the sun's reflection.

467
00:36:10,273 --> 00:36:12,317
You can ask Brother
to give you a few of these.

468
00:36:17,655 --> 00:36:19,073
[gunshot]

469
00:36:19,449 --> 00:36:21,534
In order to prepare for hacker attacks,

470
00:36:21,618 --> 00:36:25,914
we maintain our security by switching
the site cover every 72 hours.

471
00:36:32,921 --> 00:36:35,089
Click the invisible button
under the event tag

472
00:36:35,173 --> 00:36:37,258
and it'll reveal the login
to the real site.

473
00:36:37,342 --> 00:36:39,636
When you log in
using the three biometric credentials

474
00:36:39,719 --> 00:36:43,097
that you originally registered with,
along with the code,

475
00:36:44,224 --> 00:36:46,810
you will get access
to the real murthehelp.

476
00:36:47,769 --> 00:36:50,146
What'd you do? Why'd you get denied?

477
00:36:50,772 --> 00:36:52,148
Poor circulation.

478
00:37:01,908 --> 00:37:04,160
[♪ upbeat music continues]

479
00:37:04,661 --> 00:37:07,497
[Jian and Minhye grunting]
STYLE
::cue()

480
00:37:16,673 --> 00:37:17,966
No!

481
00:37:20,176 --> 00:37:22,637
[panting]

482
00:37:25,723 --> 00:37:27,433
You already finished dismantling it?

483
00:37:29,936 --> 00:37:33,022
This clover protected my life
when I escaped North Korea.

484
00:37:33,106 --> 00:37:34,566
It's yours now.

485
00:37:34,649 --> 00:37:35,984
You're giving it to me?

486
00:37:36,067 --> 00:37:39,445
My wishes all came true already.
I don't need it anymore.

487
00:37:43,783 --> 00:37:45,869
[Jian] Thank you, as always, Director Kim.

488
00:37:46,786 --> 00:37:51,291
Let's begin the new company agreement
between Jaewon Co. Ltd. and murthehelp.

489
00:37:53,001 --> 00:37:55,753
[gunfire]

490
00:38:11,644 --> 00:38:12,645
[gunfire]

491
00:38:12,729 --> 00:38:14,022
-[♪ music ends]
-This way, hurry.

492
00:38:18,610 --> 00:38:19,652
[shushes]

493
00:38:21,654 --> 00:38:25,825
This place is a place only the boss
and I know about.

494
00:38:41,591 --> 00:38:44,594
Jeong Jian, listen well.

495
00:38:45,929 --> 00:38:51,184
This place is a secret passage
you can use to escape in an emergency.

496
00:38:51,267 --> 00:38:53,603
You have to go in about 300 meters.

497
00:38:53,686 --> 00:38:56,522
When you reach the 250-meter mark,

498
00:38:56,606 --> 00:38:58,858
you can slam
the blast door shut behind you.

499
00:38:59,943 --> 00:39:01,736
What's at the end of it?

500
00:39:01,819 --> 00:39:02,946
The exit?

501
00:39:03,029 --> 00:39:06,616
Oh, right. In front of it,
there's a small room.

502
00:39:06,699 --> 00:39:08,952
Like the old shopping mall.

503
00:39:09,035 --> 00:39:10,411
From there, you can just…

504
00:39:10,995 --> 00:39:12,246
[mimics fire whooshing]

505
00:39:12,705 --> 00:39:15,041
burn the whole shopping mall down.

506
00:39:15,124 --> 00:39:17,001
-Why?
-Why?

507
00:39:17,085 --> 00:39:20,380
You're escaping through means
that it's an emergency situation

508
00:39:20,463 --> 00:39:22,590
and you can't leave any traces behind.

509
00:39:34,060 --> 00:39:37,271
[♪ eerie music playing]

510
00:39:46,489 --> 00:39:49,534
[Jian panting]

511
00:39:56,207 --> 00:39:57,458
[Jian] Eonni.

512
00:39:59,127 --> 00:40:04,632
Do you think it's gonna be hard for me
to live a normal life like everybody else?

513
00:40:09,053 --> 00:40:10,054
[Minhye] Jinman…

514
00:40:11,848 --> 00:40:16,019
am I going to have a hard time living
a normal life like everyone else?

515
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:21,399
-[gunshot echoing]
-[people screaming]

516
00:40:24,610 --> 00:40:27,488
[♪ somber music playing]

517
00:40:30,366 --> 00:40:33,995
[in Chinese] You fucking bitch.
Who on Earth are you?

518
00:40:35,788 --> 00:40:36,831
[Minhye] You don't remember?

519
00:40:37,582 --> 00:40:41,627
I am the fucking bitch
that you sold for 100 dollars.

520
00:40:43,463 --> 00:40:45,673
-[gunshot ringing]
-[bullet casing clattering]

521
00:40:46,507 --> 00:40:47,508
[Jinman, in English] Yeah.

522
00:40:49,302 --> 00:40:50,344
Probably.

523
00:40:51,471 --> 00:40:53,431
You won't be able
to live like everyone else.
STYLE
::cue()

524
00:40:54,098 --> 00:40:55,475
It's not possible, Jian.

525
00:40:59,103 --> 00:41:03,232
But… luckily,
your uncle is still alive and well.

526
00:41:05,735 --> 00:41:08,071
And there are people
who want to protect you.

527
00:41:09,822 --> 00:41:12,617
We eat meals together,
spend time together.

528
00:41:13,409 --> 00:41:14,869
Like you're doing with me right now.

529
00:41:17,663 --> 00:41:18,748
Maybe…

530
00:41:20,416 --> 00:41:21,834
this is our own kind of normal.

531
00:41:32,595 --> 00:41:33,638
[grunts]

532
00:41:56,452 --> 00:41:57,954
[Jian grunts, groans]

533
00:41:58,079 --> 00:42:00,706
-[Jian] What is this?
-What do you mean, what is this?

534
00:42:00,790 --> 00:42:03,376
The enemy will take advantage
of your weakness.

535
00:42:03,459 --> 00:42:04,877
You gotta keep your head together.

536
00:42:06,045 --> 00:42:07,046
[grunts]

537
00:42:08,089 --> 00:42:09,632
[exhales sharply]

538
00:42:26,649 --> 00:42:27,650
What?

539
00:42:28,317 --> 00:42:29,652
What are you doing here at this hour?

540
00:42:29,735 --> 00:42:33,197
Jian told me to come.
She called a meeting.

541
00:42:33,281 --> 00:42:34,282
What?

542
00:42:37,410 --> 00:42:38,578
Huh?

543
00:42:43,082 --> 00:42:45,293
[♪ tense music playing]

544
00:42:46,085 --> 00:42:47,545
Everyone is here.

545
00:42:51,632 --> 00:42:53,551
I gave things some serious thought.

546
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:55,887
This man.

547
00:42:59,891 --> 00:43:02,977
-[Jin] The server administrator?
-[K] Yes.

548
00:43:03,060 --> 00:43:04,854
One of the prior administrators

549
00:43:04,937 --> 00:43:07,690
happened to be on the bus
that we ordered to be exploded.

550
00:43:07,773 --> 00:43:09,859
-So we hired a new one.
-Okay.

551
00:43:09,942 --> 00:43:12,653
-You vetted him thoroughly, right?
-Yes.

552
00:43:28,753 --> 00:43:30,630
Who was that man?

553
00:43:30,713 --> 00:43:33,090
Head of security
during Lee Yonghan's time here.

554
00:43:33,174 --> 00:43:34,467
Oh…

555
00:43:34,675 --> 00:43:38,262
He let Jeong Jinman get away,
lost the server, and yet here he is.

556
00:43:38,346 --> 00:43:39,597
[K] I'll take care of it.

557
00:43:42,141 --> 00:43:43,517
What is it now?

558
00:43:47,855 --> 00:43:48,981
Negotiate?

559
00:43:56,948 --> 00:43:59,909
They made the offer first?

560
00:43:59,992 --> 00:44:01,702
[in Korean] Yes. No.

561
00:44:04,789 --> 00:44:06,040
[in English] Yes.

562
00:44:11,754 --> 00:44:13,881
[Jin exhales deeply]

563
00:44:14,507 --> 00:44:16,926
What are you playing at, Jeong Jinman?

564
00:44:19,387 --> 00:44:21,055
So where are we doing this?
STYLE
::cue()

565
00:44:57,925 --> 00:45:00,261
[truck rumbling]

566
00:45:05,224 --> 00:45:07,768
[♪ tense music playing]

567
00:45:17,403 --> 00:45:19,238
[truck door clanks]

568
00:46:03,616 --> 00:46:05,117
Where is Jeong Jinman?

569
00:46:06,118 --> 00:46:07,578
Jeong Jinman's not coming.

570
00:46:09,830 --> 00:46:13,292
[♪ tense music continues]

571
00:46:15,753 --> 00:46:17,088
I'm Jeong Jian.

572
00:46:18,089 --> 00:46:20,341
I will be doing the negotiating.

573
00:46:24,470 --> 00:46:26,097
You're breaking your promise again.

574
00:46:26,806 --> 00:46:29,058
Do you think we're playing
some kind of game here?

575
00:46:31,602 --> 00:46:32,812
You are the one…

576
00:46:34,397 --> 00:46:35,898
playing games.

577
00:46:41,028 --> 00:46:43,823
[screams] Aren't you, Ms. Kusanagi?

578
00:46:50,913 --> 00:46:54,166
The CEO came in person on our side.
It's uneven.

579
00:46:56,419 --> 00:46:59,880
The status level should match
in negotiation, but there is…

580
00:47:00,589 --> 00:47:02,591
a proxy instead of you.

581
00:47:04,677 --> 00:47:06,887
[doors whirring]

582
00:47:22,903 --> 00:47:25,614
[♪ sinister music playing]

583
00:47:54,977 --> 00:47:56,395
[Q] This is your last chance.

584
00:47:57,855 --> 00:48:01,609
If you don't come with me,
your boyfriend will also die.

585
00:48:02,151 --> 00:48:05,029
[heartbeat thumps rapidly]
STYLE
::cue()

586
00:48:16,040 --> 00:48:17,208
[scoffs]

587
00:48:18,584 --> 00:48:19,960
You two have met before.

588
00:48:20,961 --> 00:48:23,214
You remember, don't you?

589
00:48:24,965 --> 00:48:27,092
In order to match my status level,

590
00:48:27,176 --> 00:48:30,262
Jeong Jinman would need to be
the one sitting in front of me.

591
00:48:30,346 --> 00:48:32,389
But it's fine.

592
00:48:32,473 --> 00:48:35,100
You and I are lucky
to live in today's world,

593
00:48:35,184 --> 00:48:38,646
a world where a young lady like you
can become a CEO.

594
00:48:40,481 --> 00:48:41,690
Like me.

595
00:48:55,955 --> 00:48:57,957
[♪ suspenseful tense music playing]

596
00:48:58,999 --> 00:49:01,961
Ms. Kusanagi, I apologize

597
00:49:03,045 --> 00:49:06,423
for the damage caused to Babylon
over the past two years.

598
00:49:06,882 --> 00:49:09,885
[laughs]

599
00:49:12,304 --> 00:49:13,639
I'll accept that.

600
00:49:13,722 --> 00:49:16,100
I'd hardly call that damage, though.

601
00:49:16,183 --> 00:49:19,103
It doesn't even scratch the surface
compared to what you've been through.

602
00:49:19,186 --> 00:49:21,313
You lost your parents when you were seven

603
00:49:21,397 --> 00:49:24,942
and found out what your uncle really did
for a living when you became an adult.

604
00:49:25,025 --> 00:49:27,987
Not to mention the day you survived
the carnage in your home.

605
00:49:29,530 --> 00:49:32,241
Do you remember when you shot the drone
with your slingshot?

606
00:49:32,324 --> 00:49:34,118
-[Jin chuckles]
-Hm.

607
00:49:34,618 --> 00:49:36,537
We were expecting to meet with Jinman.

608
00:49:36,620 --> 00:49:40,374
Our intention was to hold him responsible
for Babylon's losses.

609
00:49:41,166 --> 00:49:42,918
But his niece showed up instead.

610
00:49:43,586 --> 00:49:44,878
That's too bad.

611
00:49:44,962 --> 00:49:46,755
Well, I'm the one here.

612
00:49:48,257 --> 00:49:50,509
You're going to have to negotiate with me.

613
00:49:53,637 --> 00:49:55,389
Oh, yeah? Why would we do that?

614
00:49:55,472 --> 00:49:57,641
Starting this very minute,

615
00:49:57,725 --> 00:50:00,436
Jeong Jinman is no longer involved
with murthehelp.

616
00:50:00,519 --> 00:50:02,187
He's officially stepped down.

617
00:50:05,190 --> 00:50:07,318
This vicious cycle of fighting
will keep repeating

618
00:50:07,401 --> 00:50:09,361
as long as Jeong Jinman is involved.

619
00:50:09,445 --> 00:50:13,407
The problem is that his style of operation
always uses force with force.

620
00:50:16,493 --> 00:50:18,495
If the fighting never stops…

621
00:50:21,957 --> 00:50:23,876
both sides will continue to lose.

622
00:50:26,211 --> 00:50:28,464
I want us to coexist together.

623
00:50:28,547 --> 00:50:30,841
I'm proposing we form a partnership.

624
00:50:30,924 --> 00:50:33,594
Murthehelp and Babylon working together.

625
00:50:33,677 --> 00:50:35,137
As we hand over the server,

626
00:50:35,220 --> 00:50:38,307
we'll also be sharing
murthehelp's business with Babylon.

627
00:50:38,390 --> 00:50:39,475
You can stop…

628
00:50:42,186 --> 00:50:43,479
[clears throat]

629
00:50:44,063 --> 00:50:48,233
No need to bother making knock-offs,
like that half-baked app you made.

630
00:50:48,317 --> 00:50:51,779
Instead, we'll share the profits
and prioritize Babylon's weapons

631
00:50:51,862 --> 00:50:54,114
in our Sales and Distribution departments.

632
00:50:54,198 --> 00:50:56,533
Also, if over time,

633
00:50:57,326 --> 00:51:00,037
we feel that there's enough trust
built between us,

634
00:51:00,120 --> 00:51:04,708
we might even be open to the possibility
of selling murthehelp entirely to Babylon

635
00:51:04,792 --> 00:51:06,168
at a reasonable price.

636
00:51:07,211 --> 00:51:08,253
M and A.

637
00:51:09,296 --> 00:51:10,381
That sound good?

638
00:51:11,715 --> 00:51:12,800
[server admin, in Japanese]
He says they haven't breached anything

639
00:51:12,883 --> 00:51:13,967
other than the exposed data.

640
00:51:14,802 --> 00:51:16,720
They've only breached the exposed data.

641
00:51:21,016 --> 00:51:22,184
And your terms?

642
00:51:22,685 --> 00:51:25,104
[♪ suspenseful tense music continues]

643
00:51:25,729 --> 00:51:26,730
They're simple.

644
00:51:27,731 --> 00:51:28,816
Jeong Jinman.

645
00:51:31,235 --> 00:51:33,362
Nobody's allowed to touch him from now on.

646
00:51:34,738 --> 00:51:39,785
In other words, you are asking us
to spare your uncle's life.

647
00:51:42,746 --> 00:51:44,081
In so many words.

648
00:51:50,129 --> 00:51:51,588
This is the key to the truck.

649
00:51:51,672 --> 00:51:55,676
If you pick it up, I'll consider it
as you accepting my offer.

650
00:51:55,759 --> 00:51:58,637
You're very bold
in begging for Jinman's life.

651
00:52:02,141 --> 00:52:06,186
If you brought me ten of Jinman's heads
wrapped in a tiny little bow,
STYLE
::cue()

652
00:52:06,270 --> 00:52:07,730
it still wouldn't be enough.

653
00:52:09,732 --> 00:52:10,816
If I refuse?

654
00:52:14,361 --> 00:52:15,571
Then…

655
00:52:18,490 --> 00:52:19,742
we'll all…

656
00:52:20,993 --> 00:52:22,077
die right here.

657
00:52:22,828 --> 00:52:25,038
-[alarm blares]
-[guns clicking]

658
00:52:30,335 --> 00:52:31,879
See those bombs?

659
00:52:31,962 --> 00:52:34,047
They're linked to my biometric signal.

660
00:52:34,131 --> 00:52:35,841
The moment that signal's cut…

661
00:52:35,924 --> 00:52:37,426
[slams table]

662
00:52:37,968 --> 00:52:39,052
…they'll detonate.

663
00:52:43,348 --> 00:52:44,975
Maybe it's because you're young,

664
00:52:45,768 --> 00:52:47,394
you're not afraid of dying.

665
00:52:49,229 --> 00:52:50,731
You're so reckless.

666
00:52:53,776 --> 00:52:54,818
Dying?

667
00:52:55,986 --> 00:52:57,988
I don't care about that anymore.

668
00:52:58,906 --> 00:53:00,407
I'm beyond that now.

669
00:53:02,868 --> 00:53:05,370
I already died once on that island.

670
00:53:06,288 --> 00:53:08,874
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

671
00:53:10,334 --> 00:53:11,418
Are you scared?

672
00:53:17,090 --> 00:53:18,133
Let's hear it.

673
00:53:20,761 --> 00:53:21,845
Is dying…

674
00:53:23,847 --> 00:53:25,641
something you're afraid of?

675
00:53:28,101 --> 00:53:29,144
Lights!

676
00:53:32,356 --> 00:53:34,191
[Seongbeom] Switch to infrared now.

677
00:53:40,405 --> 00:53:42,032
I've long wondered

678
00:53:42,991 --> 00:53:46,578
how you survived
those impossible situations.

679
00:53:47,871 --> 00:53:51,542
Seeing you now, I finally understand.

680
00:53:55,420 --> 00:53:57,798
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

681
00:54:03,220 --> 00:54:06,306
See you soon, Jeong Jian.

682
00:54:31,456 --> 00:54:32,457
[exhales]

683
00:54:55,856 --> 00:54:57,149
[exhales sharply]

684
00:55:00,694 --> 00:55:03,322
-I appreciate it.
-Fuck that bullshit.

685
00:55:05,490 --> 00:55:08,493
Jeong Jinman,
I didn't come because I like you.

686
00:55:08,577 --> 00:55:11,038
I broke my promise to your niece
that one day.

687
00:55:11,872 --> 00:55:13,332
But now I've paid my debt.

688
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:19,046
I'm done with murthehelp and code shit
and anything related to it.

689
00:55:20,213 --> 00:55:23,467
-Forget about me.
-I appreciate it, regardless.

690
00:55:25,594 --> 00:55:26,595
Let's go.

691
00:55:35,646 --> 00:55:39,066
[♪ gentle music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

692
00:55:43,654 --> 00:55:46,156
[Cheolseung]
When you shouted "Ms. Kusanagi,"

693
00:55:46,239 --> 00:55:48,325
you scared the living hell out of me.

694
00:55:48,408 --> 00:55:50,202
[Jian] When did I do that?

695
00:55:50,285 --> 00:55:52,287
[Cheolseung] Little Jian was so cool.

696
00:55:52,371 --> 00:55:54,331
[Minhye] She really has
grown into herself.

697
00:55:54,414 --> 00:55:56,500
[Cheolseung] Hey, how did you know
it was a camera?

698
00:55:56,583 --> 00:56:00,754
-I just looked and saw it.
-Oh, your bloodline is strong.

699
00:56:01,338 --> 00:56:03,507
[chuckles] Hurry up and eat. It's done.

700
00:56:03,590 --> 00:56:06,802
[Brother] Don't eat it all!
Leave me some too!

701
00:56:06,885 --> 00:56:09,846
[Jinwoo] Oh, man, our Brother is
a samgyeopsal killer. What a shame!

702
00:56:09,930 --> 00:56:12,015
[Cheolseung] Hey, just
stuff your face with ramyeon.

703
00:56:12,099 --> 00:56:14,101
-Challenge!
-[Jian] Finish up there and come down.

704
00:56:14,768 --> 00:56:16,353
They're rubbing it in.

705
00:56:17,145 --> 00:56:20,649
-Code Blue?
-Transport is really important.

706
00:56:20,732 --> 00:56:24,528
We have to deliver the products
to the target locations discreetly,

707
00:56:24,611 --> 00:56:27,030
but right now
each code handles them directly.

708
00:56:28,240 --> 00:56:31,535
By creating a new code
that specializes in transportation,

709
00:56:31,618 --> 00:56:34,871
I think it would really help us
down the line, don't you?

710
00:56:35,831 --> 00:56:36,957
What do you think?

711
00:56:39,793 --> 00:56:40,877
Why look at me?

712
00:56:41,878 --> 00:56:43,839
Murthehelp's CEO is Jeong Jian.

713
00:56:43,922 --> 00:56:47,217
If she says we should do it,
then we do it.

714
00:56:47,968 --> 00:56:49,553
Okay. Good.

715
00:56:49,636 --> 00:56:51,221
I'm Code Blue number one.

716
00:56:51,304 --> 00:56:53,473
I always fly the helicopter
or drive the car.

717
00:56:53,557 --> 00:56:55,767
-I handle all transportation, right?
-[Jian] No.

718
00:56:55,851 --> 00:56:59,396
-Uncle Jinwoo, you can't be Code Blue.
-Why not?

719
00:56:59,479 --> 00:57:00,689
One more thing.

720
00:57:01,648 --> 00:57:03,775
I would like if all of us here…

721
00:57:06,194 --> 00:57:07,404
Brother included.

722
00:57:10,323 --> 00:57:12,033
Everybody at this table,

723
00:57:12,701 --> 00:57:16,830
becomes Code Green from now on.

724
00:57:18,707 --> 00:57:19,750
What?

725
00:57:22,127 --> 00:57:25,464
It's only natural. You're all important.

726
00:57:26,173 --> 00:57:27,966
We've all become like family now.

727
00:57:28,049 --> 00:57:30,051
It's only right that you're Code Green.

728
00:57:30,135 --> 00:57:33,972
That means that Uncle Jinwoo,
you're not Code Blue. You're Code Green.

729
00:57:35,807 --> 00:57:37,058
Minhye Eonni.

730
00:57:39,519 --> 00:57:41,146
Uncle Cheolseung, you too.

731
00:57:42,939 --> 00:57:45,984
[♪ gentle music playing]

732
00:57:46,443 --> 00:57:47,861
[Jinman clears throat]

733
00:57:56,036 --> 00:57:57,746
This suddenly…

734
00:57:58,622 --> 00:58:02,125
reminds me of my mother
that I had to leave behind in North Korea.

735
00:58:04,544 --> 00:58:07,047
I haven't heard that word
since coming to the South.

736
00:58:08,298 --> 00:58:09,299
Family.

737
00:58:10,509 --> 00:58:11,968
Thank you, Jian.

738
00:58:14,721 --> 00:58:17,849
Hey, come on. Let's drink to that.
Yeah? Huh?

739
00:58:17,974 --> 00:58:19,476
-[Jinwoo] Okay. In one shot!
-[Jinman] Here.

740
00:58:20,685 --> 00:58:24,022
Our hearts to the motherland,
our livers to our comrades.

741
00:58:24,105 --> 00:58:25,899
-[Cheolseung] Cheers!
-[Jinwoo] Cans up.

742
00:58:25,982 --> 00:58:27,025
[all] Cheers.

743
00:58:28,235 --> 00:58:30,570
[all exhaling sharply]

744
00:58:30,695 --> 00:58:33,657
[Cheolseung] If we don't celebrate on
a day like today, when will we ever, huh?

745
00:58:33,740 --> 00:58:35,951
[Jinwoo] You're right. That's right. Wow!

746
00:58:36,034 --> 00:58:37,744
Comrade's saying
all the right things today.

747
00:58:37,828 --> 00:58:39,412
-[Jinwoo] Hey, take a photo.
-[Cheolseung] Yeah, good idea.

748
00:58:39,496 --> 00:58:40,497
[camera shutter clicks]

749
00:58:40,580 --> 00:58:41,915
Pasin.

750
00:58:43,875 --> 00:58:46,628
[Pasin weakly] Help me, Jinman.

751
00:58:46,711 --> 00:58:51,466
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

752
00:58:51,925 --> 00:58:53,176
[Jin] Jeong Jian…

753
00:58:54,219 --> 00:58:55,929
That little kid was cute.

754
00:58:56,721 --> 00:58:59,558
She must have thought
I really went to negotiate.

755
00:59:02,143 --> 00:59:06,022
-[blows landing]
-[Pasin groaning, coughing]

756
00:59:09,192 --> 00:59:14,573
So, in return, you are going to have
to do a little work for us.

757
00:59:16,741 --> 00:59:19,119
[screams]

758
00:59:20,745 --> 00:59:23,707
[♪ closing theme music playing]

759
00:59:27,752 --> 00:59:29,212
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG

